# A loop body ending in the wrong type.
#
# What the body ends in is what the next turn carries, so it is checked
# against the accumulator exactly as a binding's value is checked
# against its annotation. Here the loop carries an Int and its body ends
# in a Bool.
#
# This program is expected to FAIL type checking. Its `.ast.out` holds
# the error message, not a program's output.

counted = loop x = 1:
    if x > 3:
        break
    x > 0
